<section id="sec-intro" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>5-12-13 Triangle Calculator</h2>
  <p>Scale a 5-12-13 triangle and find its sides, area, and perimeter.</p>
  <p>A 5-12-13 triangle is a right triangle whose side lengths follow the ratio <span set:html={rich('[[5 : 12 : 13]]')} />. It is a Pythagorean triple, because its whole-number sides satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: <span set:html={rich('[[5^2 + 12^2 = 13^2]]')} />, since <span set:html={rich('[[25 + 144 = 169]]')} />. The side of length 13 is the hypotenuse, and the sides of length 5 and 12 are the legs that meet at the right angle.</p>
  <p>The calculator scales that triangle by a positive scale factor <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} />, so the scaled sides are <span set:html={rich('[[a = 5k]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b = 12k]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[c = 13k]]')} />. It also works out the area, <span set:html={rich('[[A = 30k^2]]')} />, and the perimeter, <span set:html={rich('[[P = 30k]]')} />, so one input gives all five results. Use the <a href="/right-triangle-calculator/">right triangle calculator</a> for a general right triangle.</p>
  <p>For example, with <span set:html={rich('[[k = 2]]')} /> the sides become <span set:html={rich('[[a = 10]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b = 24]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[c = 26]]')} />, the area is <span set:html={rich('[[A = 120]]')} /> square units, and the perimeter is <span set:html={rich('[[P = 60]]')} /> units.</p>
</section>

