  <p>The scale factor is the number that stretches or shrinks the original triangle. With <span set:html={rich('[[k = 1]]')} /> you get the original 5, 12, 13 triangle. With <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> greater than 1 the triangle grows, and with <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> between 0 and 1 it shrinks, but the shape never changes.</p>
  <p>Every result comes from the same <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} />, so the five outputs always agree with each other. If <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> is zero or negative, the calculator will not accept it, because zero gives a degenerate figure and negative values cannot describe side lengths.</p>
